ment, so it doesn't need `auth.json` and starts each run from an empty `CODEX_HOME`. This also means your `~/.codex/config.toml` (model, profiles, MCP servers) is **not** used here. If the plain `codex` lane depends on settings in it, the two lanes won't be exactly the same. To fix that, put a copy of the config in the scratch `.codex` or pass the settings with `-c`.","+- **Where `final.txt` gets written.** `codex -o` is written by Codex from inside the sandbox. On the eval Mac the repo is in `~/evals/agent-evals`, which is under the real home, so writing directly to `runs/...` would be blocked. The lane writes `final.txt` into the scratch HOME and copies it to the run folder afterwards. `agent.log` and `agent.err` are fine as they are, because the shell opens those redirects outside the sandbox.","+- **Codex's built-in sandbox is still turned off** (`--dangerously-bypass-approvals-and-sandbox`), as in the `codex` lane. Codex's own sandbox is Seatbelt too, and `sandbox-exec` can't run inside another sandbox. `agent.sb` takes its place.","+- **Network access is open**, same as in `kimi`.","+","+## Verification","+","+- `bash -n run.sh` passes.","+- I ran the lane's exact sandbox setup with a probe script in place of the agent.","+  - With the `codex-sandboxed` parameters:","+    - blocked: reading `~/.codex/auth.json`, listing `~/.codex`, reading `~/.kimi-code`, and writing a file in `~`;","+    - allowed: writing to the scratch HOME and to the work folder, and running `codex --version` and `timeout`.","+  - With the `kimi` parameters, the only change is that reading `~/.kimi-code` is allowed, which is the same as before the change.","+- **Not done:** a real end-to-end run. `CODEX_API_KEY` isn't set on this machine, and a run would send the prompt to OpenAI. The first real run is `./run.sh fizz codex-sandboxed`. Check that `runs/fizz-codex-sandboxed-r1/answer.json` has a non-empty `final` and that `agent.err` has no `Operation not permitted`."]}],"created":true},{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-hntv3B/README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":17,"oldLines":6,"newStart":17,"newLines":9,"lines":[" Lanes:"," "," - `codex`: Codex CLI (`codex exec --json`), unsandboxed.","+- `codex-sandboxed`: the same Codex run as `codex`, but under","+  `sandbox/agent.sb` like `kimi`, with an empty scratch HOME and `CODEX_HOME`","+  (nothing in the real home is opened, not even `~/.codex`)."," - `kimi`: Kimi Code. Its output goes to Moonshot, so its shell runs under the","   macOS sandbox profile `sandbox/agent.sb` (no reading or writing the real","   home), with an empty scratch HOME. Kimi's own install and sessions live in"]}]}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/private/tmp/h-hntv3B/ANSWER.md","/private/tmp/h-hntv3B/README.md"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ThcABxk3j9EUaqAnrBsFEU","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
